n\\\\nSo the only possible order is:  \\\\n**Pia - Rhea - Xena**\\\\n\\\\nSo we have a triplet: **Pia, Rhea, Xena** in that order, with Rhea between Pia and Xena, and Pia to the left of Rhea.\\\\n\\\\nThey don’t have to be adjacent, but Rhea is between them.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 2: Use clue 7: Iris sat between Pia and Xena\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris is between Pia and Xena.\\\\n\\\\nWe already have Pia - Rhea - Xena, so Pia and Xena are on opposite sides of Rhea.\\\\n\\\\nNow, Iris is between Pia and Xena → So Iris must be somewhere between Pia and Xena.\\\\n\\\\nBut we already have Rhea between Pia and Xena.\\\\n\\\\nSo both Rhea and Iris are between Pia and Xena.\\\\n\\\\nSo the order must be: Pia, then Iris, then Rhea, then Xena? Or Pia, then Rhea, then Iris, then Xena? Or Pia, then Iris, then Xena, with Rhea somewhere in between?\\\\n\\\\nWait — we already have from clue 2 and 3: **Pia - Rhea - Xena** (with Rhea between Pia and Xena, and Pia < Rhea)\\\\n\\\\nNow clue 7: Iris is between Pia and Xena → So Pia < Iris < Xena\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris is somewhere between Pia and Xena.\\\\n\\\\nBut we already have Rhea between Pia and Xena.\\\\n\\\\nSo both Rhea and Iris are between Pia and Xena.\\\\n\\\\nSo the order must be: Pia, then Iris, then Rhea, then Xena? Or Pia, then Rhea, then Iris, then Xena? Or Pia, then Iris, then Xena, with Rhea between Pia and Xena?\\\\n\\\\nBut Rhea must be between Pia and Xena, so Rhea is somewhere between Pia and Xena.\\\\n\\\\nIris is also between Pia and Xena.\\\\n\\\\nSo both are in the interval (Pia, Xena).\\\\n\\\\nBut we also have clue 1: Iris and Xena are next to each other.\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris is adjacent to Xena.\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris is immediately to the left of Xena.\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris is in seat n, Xena in seat n+1.\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris is adjacent to Xena.\\\\n\\\\nSo from clue 7: Iris is between\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"length\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794483187,