3. Good.\\\\n\\\\nThen Vera between Jun and Sami. V position k+2. Sami > D > F = k, so S >= k+2? D > k, S > D. V = k+2. For V between Jun and S: either J < V < S or S < V < J. Since S > D > F. S could be > V or maybe S=?? D position > k, S > D. If D=k+1? But k+1 is Z occupied, impossible. D cannot be k+1. D could be k+3? occupied C, or later. S > D. If D >= k+3, S >= k+4 > V. So S > V. Unless D? D cannot be k+1, k+2 V, k+3 C, so D >= k+4, S>=k+5. Thus S > V. Therefore Vera between Jun and Sami implies J < V < S. So Jun left of V. But block starts at k with F at k. Jun must be left of V and not in block positions k..k+3. The only possible seat left of V not in block? If k>1, seats < k available. Jun must be < k. If k=1 no seat left for Jun. So k >=2. Also D/S to right of C maybe.\\\\n\\\\nRemaining after block F,Z,V,C occupying k..k+3: D, S, J plus maybe empty? There are 7 seats, block length 4. Need J < k. D,S > k and D<S, with D not in block. Since seats k+1,k+2,k+3 occupied, D/S must be in seats k+4..7 (two seats) if available. Need two seats right of block. Thus k+4 <=7 => k<=3. And J one seat left of k. So k=2 or3? If k=2, block seats2-5, right seats6,7 for D,S, left seat1 for J. Works. If k=3, block seats3-6\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"length\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794483187,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":198,\\\"total_tokens\\\":1198,\\\"completion_tokens\\\":1000,\\\"prompt_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"cached_tokens\\\":0},\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":1003,\\\"completion_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":1003}}}\",\"signature\":{\"text\":\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:b192aef1816219782ef88272d0a75bccc8e51a3d54cf7507a692a24c9aa8dfe3:73cedccbc87a9e627b9f57bebca8996e5d78c4f3553cc66b4e696fd5a7019493\",\"signature\":\"0x11a7dbe020e159a1dc09b73392fbcc152588625a5e07a7a921be6c0f1271a6fb6dfe0cd4b9d0c4a667f1d0146950308b08792f52138c706c5810c5498e6825681b\",\"signing_address\":\"0x3b753b4406613c5e70ae6405086